## Goal

Run the next held-out mechanism ablation described in `evals/v0.2-ablation.md`.

Compare:
- Raw DeepSeek
- Deep Native v0.1 at `fda3dd010e7de8f8c1ee1953e006e577464aa3d6`
- Deep Native v0.2 Candidate at current `main`

## Scope

Four held-out task families only:
1. hard root-cause debugging;
2. environment failure classification;
3. fresh verification after a relevant post-check edit;
4. recovery after real code progress and an actual new session.

First stage: 12 total runs. Do not expand to 60 unless the 12-run trace review shows a mechanism-level reason to continue.

## Guardrails

- preflight writable temp/heredoc/mktemp behavior before model calls;
- freeze tasks before running;
- same Claude Code, DeepSeek model, permissions, prompt, budget, and clean starting workspace across arms;
- no tuning v0.2 against frozen tasks and then reusing them as held-out evidence;
- retain failures and raw traces;
- no model-parity claim from this ablation.

## Deliverable

Machine-readable results, trace review, environment audit, concise report, and a CONTINUE / ANALYZE / STOP judgment.
